Like usually, there will be as many branche as they are merge proposals to the
upstream and they will stay opened as long are they are not reviewed or accepted
or rejected.

There is a `personal-version` branch, where changes will be applied wether or
not they are applied in the upstream. Initially, the idea was to also fork this
fork, for the personal version. But this is not possible as I’m not the member
of any organization. So instead of pushing the change to the upstream and a
second fork, the change will be manually duplicated in the `personal-version`
branch and in each branch to be proposed for merging in upstream.

As an unwanted side effect, all references to issues will be duplicated.
